# fd's GLOBAL ignore file. The location is the whole point: fd's README documents
# `~/.config/fd/ignore` as the global one, while `~/.fdignore` (where this lived)
# is parent-walked like `.gitignore` and stops at the enclosing repo root — so
# inside any project it was not applying at all.
#
# `.git/` is here on fd's own advice: "You may wish to include `.git/` in your
# fd/ignore file so that `.git` directories, and their contents are not included
# in output if you use the --hidden option." Both fzf commands in
# zsh/60-tools.zsh pass --hidden, and they used to carry a duplicated
# `--exclude .git` each instead.
#
# ripgrep has no equivalent auto-loaded global file, so its half of this is
# `--glob=!.git/` in `.ripgreprc`, which is prepended to every invocation.
.git/
